  "id": "COMPOUND:18973 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "Arborescidine D appears to have a complex, multi-tiered relationship with NCI-H446, as evidenced by three distinct paths that all lead to the target NCI-H446 through different intermediates. The first path connects Arborescidine D to Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8, which is then targeted by Hexadecanedioic acid, ultimately leading to NCI-H446. The second path links Arborescidine D to VMRC-LCP, which is targeted by a complex compound, and this complex also targets NCI-H446. The third path connects Arborescidine D to MOVP-3, which is targeted by the same complex as in the second path, and this complex also targets NCI-H446. \n\nThese findings suggest that Arborescidine D may act through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving the modulation of signaling pathways or the inhibition of specific enzymes, which ultimately influence the behavior of NCI-H446. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Arborescidine D and NCI-H446, though the exact mode of action remains unclear. The presence of multiple intermediates and the involvement of complex compounds indicate that the relationship may be multifaceted, requiring further investigation to determine the precise biological mechanisms at play.",
